## Phase 22: Operate (ongoing, post-launch)


The runbook finishes at 21; the business doesn't. When the user returns after launch, run this recurring cadence instead of restarting phases. Owned by the CEO role.

| Cadence | Skill | Path |
|---------|-------|------|
| Weekly | `project-status-report` | `awesome-claude-corporate-skills/07-operations/project-status-report/` |
| Weekly | `analytics` review vs Phase 20 KPIs | `marketingskills/analytics/` |
| Monthly | `marketing-council` (critique live funnel) | `marketingskills/marketing-council/` |
| Monthly | `kaizen` / `process-optimization` | `awesome-claude-corporate-skills/07-operations/` |
| Quarterly | `board-meeting-prep` + `executive-communication` | `awesome-claude-corporate-skills/01-executive-leadership/` |
| On incident | `incident-postmortem` | `awesome-claude-corporate-skills/07-operations/incident-postmortem/` |
| On paid underperformance | `performance-diagnosis` | `advertising-skills/skills/operator-os/performance-diagnosis/` |

Each cycle: read `20-analytics.md` KPIs → report actuals vs targets → propose top 3 actions → on approval, re-open the relevant phase (e.g. weak conversion → re-run Phase 18) and log it in the tracker's decisions log.

**Output:** `22-operating-cadence.md` — living log, newest entry on top.

